[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314259285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314259285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314259285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fi5VV","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T00:06:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T00:06:17Z","body":"> so I thought: why not expose it to `Dictionary`\r\n\r\n\"Why not?\" is never a good reason to add something to Core. While the code is minimal, it has no reason to be exposed to end users in the first place. It just adds another entry to the API that users will never touch. If sizing Dictionaries is a bottleneck, then you are already using the wrong data structure and no amount of calling `reserve()` is going to save you\r\n\r\nThis is exactly the sort of improvement contemplated by the first two of our contributor best practices:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/best_practices.html#to-solve-the-problem-it-has-to-exist-in-the-first-place","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314259285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314376435","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314376435","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314376435,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FjV7z","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T01:40:27Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T02:39:45Z","body":"> \"Why not?\" is never a good reason to add something to Core.\n\nYou might have understood things wrong. Dictionary is used in countless places within the engine that can benefit from this.\n\n> While the code is minimal, it has no reason to be exposed to end users in the first place. It just adds another entry to the API that users will never touch.\n\nExcept it isn't? It's only exposed for internal use within the engine where beneficial.\n\nMy apologies if using the word \"expose\" led to wrong conclusions. I did a bit of rewording. \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314376435/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314529135","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314529135","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314529135,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fj7Nv","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T04:14:37Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T04:14:37Z","body":"That's my bad. I didn't notice that there wasn't any binding code touched. That takes away my concern about this being exposed to end users. Adding something like this for internal use is a lot less of a problem.\r\n\r\nThat being said, if it's truly a benefit. Then this PR should be using it somewhere where dictionary allocations were a problem. Remember, the problem always needs to come first. We don't add solutions to the engine and then plan on finding problems. We start by identifying a problem, then we make changes to solve that problem. \r\n\r\nThis may very well be the correct solution to _a_ problem, but in order to merge it, we need to know _what_ that problem is. \r\n\r\nIt isn't enough to say that some places _could_ benefit from this change. Show me what places _do_ benefit from this change by profiling them before and after the change. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314529135/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314532675","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314532675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314532675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fj8FD","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T04:18:12Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T04:18:12Z","body":"> If sizing Dictionaries is a bottleneck, then you are already using the wrong data structure and no amount of calling reserve() is going to save you\r\n\r\nThat seems like a bit of a nonsensical take on this particular feature. `reserve()` is a standard feature for maps in most languages, and if you know the size AOT you can optimize with a reservation, which can be significant for large dictionaries or for manual copies or transformations of large dictionaries.\r\n\r\nI would consider this a core library feature for `Dictionary` that is currently absent. Given that the cost of adding the API surface is effectively zero (as the API is a simple passthrough to the underlying `HashMap`), there would not be sufficient justification to deny it. \r\n\r\n> This may very well be the correct solution to a problem, but in order to merge it, we need to know what that problem is.\r\n\r\nYou do know what that problem is. Churn in a `HashMap` is wasteful. You don't need to have strict performance numbers for something that is this straightforward.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314532675/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314565018","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314565018","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314565018,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkD-a","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T04:57:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T05:25:41Z","body":"> This may very well be the correct solution to a problem, but in order to merge it, we need to know what that problem is.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous situations within the engine where known final size dictionaries could be built faster for basically free by reserving. Isn't this a problem?\r\n\r\nThe point is that doing everything inside a single PR would be hard to keep track of.\r\n\r\nTake #105928 for example, which does the same thing but for `Vector`, `Array` and `String`. It adds the possibility, and there are certainly more cases for that than this PR, but doesn't apply it anywhere.\r\n\r\nThe reason I did apply on the GDScript VM was mostly because that case was able to be reproduced and benchmarked within GDScript.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314565018/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314600236","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314600236","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314600236,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkMks","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T05:28:55Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T05:28:55Z","body":"> There are numerous situations within the engine where known final size dictionaries could be built faster for basically free by reserving. Isn't this a problem?\r\n\r\nSure, find one and show me. If there are numerous it should not be hard. I'm really not asking for much. \r\n\r\n> The point is that doing everything inside a single PR would be hard to keep track of.\r\n\r\nSure, don't do everything then. Just solve the low hanging fruit issues. As it stands this PR does nothing, I am asking for it to do _something_ before merging. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314600236/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314604076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314604076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314604076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkNgs","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T05:35:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T05:35:38Z","body":"> That seems like a bit of a nonsensical take on this particular feature. reserve() is a standard feature for maps in most languages, and if you know the size AOT you can optimize with a reservation, which can be significant for large dictionaries or for manual copies or transformations of large dictionaries.\r\n\r\n@Shadows-of-Fire Dictionary isn't our standard map in the engine, Hashmap is. By design we don't use Dictionary in any performance sensitive areas. Which is why I said above, if we find Dictionary in a performance sensitive areas, we are likely using the wrong data structure. \r\n\r\nAs I said above, if it's so obvious that this will fix a problem somewhere, then just find that problem and point it out. I'm not saying we shouldn't merge this, quite the contrary, I'm saying we _should_ merge it _after_ we have identified the problem it is solving and then used it to solve that problem. \r\n\r\nIf the problem is so obvious, you should have no problem finding it. To be blunt, don't waste your time arguing about whether something is useful in theory. I'm certain that 'reserve()' is useful in theory. Instead, spend your time showing where it is useful 'in practice'","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314604076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314624209","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314624209","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314624209,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkSbR","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:14:26Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T14:11:06Z","body":"A few cases I could find in `core/`, performance critical or not:\r\n- `Engine::get_version/author/copyright/donor/license_info()`\r\n- `ProjectSettings::_add_builtin_input_map()`\r\n- `Image::_get_data()`\r\n- `marshalls.cpp` (`decode_variant()`)\r\n- `PListNode::get_value()`\r\n- `ResourceLoaderBinary::parse_variant()`\r\n- `ResourceFormatLoader::rename_dependencies()`\r\n- `Resource::_duplicate_recursive()`\r\n- `AStarGrid2D::get_point_data_in_region()`\r\n- `TriangleMesh::intersect_*_scriptwrap()`\r\n- A few functions within `Object`\r\n- `Script::_get_script_constant_map()` and `ScriptServer::save_global_classes()`\r\n- `OS::get_memory_info()`\r\n- Most functions in `Time`\r\n- `TranslationPO::_get_messages()`\r\n- `Translation::_get_messages()`\r\n\r\nThe one case I applied `reserve()` in this PR should speed up Dictionary construction from GDScript, as seen in my benchmark results. And no, we can't use HashMap there as it explicitly wants a Dictionary.\r\n\r\n> As it stands this PR does nothing\r\n\r\n...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314624209/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314833145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314833145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314833145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FlFb5","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T09:10:40Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T09:53:44Z","body":"@clayjohn Growth is especially costly for hashing types, so `reserve` is especially useful. The PR currently optimizes the case of constructing dictionaries in GDScript, which sees a 8-15% gain from GDScript. This is already motivates the PR in its own right.\r\n\r\nIn general though, while we don't use `Dictionary` internally, we can expect this function to be useful when we have to construct `Dictionary` for the user (e.g. for function returns).\r\nThe main alternative would be offering copy / move constructors, which is generally better but not always feasible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314833145/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314929020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110709#issuecomment-3314929020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110709","id":3314929020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Flc18","use